# Comis memory benchmark — operator config TEMPLATE.
# Copy to scripts/bench-memory.env and fill in the values you need. The runner
# (scripts/bench-memory.sh) sources scripts/bench-memory.env automatically.
# Protocol + runbook: .planning/MEMORY_BENCHMARK_PLAN.md  (Track J / K of the design doc).
#
# scripts/bench-memory.env is git-ignored-by-convention — never commit real keys.

# ── Gate ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The harness is SKIPPED unless this is set. The runner defaults it to 1.
COMIS_BENCH=1

# ── Datasets (needed for `retrieval` / `qa` on REAL data) ────────────────────────
# A directory holding TWO files, named EXACTLY:
#   longmemeval.json  — a LongMemEval item.  Source: https://huggingface.co/datasets/xiaowu0162/longmemeval
#                       (e.g. longmemeval_s.json or longmemeval_oracle.json → rename to longmemeval.json)
#   locomo.json       — a LoCoMo sample.     Source: https://github.com/snap-research/locomo (locomo10.json → locomo.json)
# Leave COMIS_BENCH_DATA UNSET to run on the tiny vendored fixtures (this is the dry run).
#
# IMPORTANT: the current harness evaluates the FIRST item/sample of each file. Running the
# FULL public sets (all 500 LongMemEval items / 10 LoCoMo samples) needs the per-item
# iteration extension — see "J1 Runbook → Remaining code task" in MEMORY_BENCHMARK_PLAN.md.
#COMIS_BENCH_DATA=/abs/path/to/bench-data

# ── Answer LLM (REQUIRED for `qa` / `all`) ───────────────────────────────────────
# The model that answers each question from the recalled context. Use a fixed snapshot.
#COMIS_BENCH_ANSWER_PROVIDER=anthropic
#COMIS_BENCH_ANSWER_MODEL=<answer-model-id>
#COMIS_BENCH_ANSWER_API_KEY=<answer-api-key>

# ── Judge LLM (REQUIRED for `qa` / `all`) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Grades the answer against gold with a category-specific rubric (temperature 0).
# Pin a DATED snapshot for reproducibility. LongMemEval's reference judge is GPT-4o
# (>97% agreement with human experts); pin the snapshot so numbers stay comparable.
# For the head-to-head, ALSO run a second, independent judge and publish the spread.
#COMIS_BENCH_JUDGE_PROVIDER=openai
#COMIS_BENCH_JUDGE_MODEL=<judge-model-snapshot>
#COMIS_BENCH_JUDGE_API_KEY=<judge-api-key>

# ── Optional on-device lanes (measure the DEFAULT shipping config) ───────────────
# Absent → honest FTS-only retrieval (the vector + rerank lanes do not contribute).
# Set these to light up the lanes that actually ship by default.
#LLAMA_MODEL_PATH=<embedding-model.gguf or hf:...>
#LLAMA_RERANKER_MODEL_PATH=hf:gpustack/bge-reranker-v2-m3-GGUF:bge-reranker-v2-m3-Q8_0.gguf

# ── v2.8 SUITE tiers (`scripts/bench-memory.sh suite <tier>`) ────────────────────
# Run one tier by name (or `suite all`); each writes a secret-free report under
# benchmarks/results/<tier>/. Tiers: poisoning · recall-learning · trust-contradiction
# · redaction · beam · longmemeval-v2 · memoryagentbench · pref · perltqa · personamem
# · halumem. KEYLESS: recall-learning / redaction / beam (+ the external tiers when
# COMIS_BENCH_DATA is unset — they run the loader's structural proof on the vendored
# fixture). The external tiers' FULL corpora are operator-placed under COMIS_BENCH_DATA.
# Per-tier dataset source + exact filename + loader/fixture coverage: see benchmarks/DATASETS.md.
#
# BEAM 10M stretch tier (SUITE-06, skippable). Unset → only the 1M `beam` tier runs;
# set to 1 to ALSO run the 10M scale probe (slow — default CI never pays the 10M cost).
#COMIS_BENCH_BEAM_10M=1

# ── PROVE head-to-head manifest dir (`scripts/bench-memory.sh head-to-head`) ─────
# Where the KEYLESS ($0) head-to-head proving machine writes its committable PARTIAL
# manifest (head-to-head-report.json + cross-judge-spread.json + ablation-contribution-
# report.json + adapter-conformance-report.json). This is a committed benchmarks/results/
# directory pointer — NOT a secret. Unset → the runner defaults it to
# benchmarks/results/2026-06-01-phase104-prove. Set it to write a fresh dated manifest dir.
#COMIS_PROVE_REPORT_DIR=benchmarks/results/2026-06-01-phase104-prove

# ── Regression gate current manifest (`scripts/bench-memory.sh gate`, GATE-01) ───
# Path to a CURRENT run's qa-report manifest (the operator-costed pass). When set, the
# `gate` mode compares that manifest's per-category accuracy to the COMMITTED J1 baseline
# (benchmarks/results/2026-05-31-j1-baseline/qa-report.judge-a.json) and EXITS NON-ZERO on
# a real category regression (a drop below baseline beyond the tolerance band AND
# statistically significant). Unset → the gate runs only the keyless compareToBaseline
# MECHANISM proof and claims NO regression-pass. This is a committed-results PATH pointer,
# NOT a secret. The costed `qa`/`all` run writes its manifest to $COMIS_BENCH_DATA/qa-report.json,
# so the costed gate typically points here:
#COMIS_GATE_CURRENT_MANIFEST=/abs/path/to/bench-data/qa-report.json
